  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries meaningful signal for this task. If image features are uninformative, the entire multimodal branch (~34 configs) can be deprioritized, saving substantial budget. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest test of this question: it keeps the profile setting identical to config_001 (singleprofile) and uses a standard, well-calibrated image encoder, so any accuracy difference is attributable primarily to the modality switch rather than confounded by aggregation or fusion choices. This single experiment partitions the search space into two very different strategies (RNA-centric vs. image-informative) and is therefore the highest-information next step under a tight budget."
}

